{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-59336","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88700","text":"delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-59337","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88701","text":"OS-006 Governance Shim — authorization kernel for the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]},{"id":"blk-59338","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88702","text":"Issues signed, expiring "},{"id":"spn-88703","marks":["code"],"text":"AuthorizationBlock"},{"id":"spn-88704","text":"s to destructive edges in OS-011 "},{"id":"spn-88705","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"},{"id":"spn-88706","text":" replay flows. Policy-based, deny-by-default, pluggable policy store."}]},{"id":"blk-59339","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88707","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-59340","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88708","marks":["bold"],"text":"Library:"},{"id":"spn-88709","text":" v0.1.0 production-ready"}]}],"id":"blk-59341","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59344","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88710","marks":["bold"],"text":"Tests:"},{"id":"spn-88711","text":" 42/42 (25 unit + 3 integration + 14 MCP tool tests) + 2 body-os end-to-end integration tests"}]}],"id":"blk-59343","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59346","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88712","marks":["bold"],"text":"Storage:"},{"id":"spn-88713","text":" in-memory ETS-backed "},{"id":"spn-88714","marks":["code"],"text":"PolicyStore"},{"id":"spn-88715","text":" — Postgres-backed adapter is a future additive release"}]}],"id":"blk-59345","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59348","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88716","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP server:"},{"id":"spn-88717","text":" shipped — 6 tools on the "},{"id":"spn-88718","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic"},{"id":"spn-88719","text":" namespace (put/get/list/delete policy + authorize + verify) with Anubis stdio/HTTP transport"}]}],"id":"blk-59347","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88720","marks":["bold"],"text":"Deployment:"},{"id":"spn-88721","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88722","marks":["code"],"text":"fly.toml"},{"id":"spn-88723","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-88724","marks":["code"],"text":"Dockerfile"},{"id":"spn-88725","text":" ready for Fly.io ("},{"id":"spn-88726","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic-mcp"},{"id":"spn-88727","text":", port 4400)"}]}],"id":"blk-59349","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-59351","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88728","text":"MCP surface"}]},{"id":"blk-59352","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"delegatic_put_policy       — register or replace a Policy\ndelegatic_get_policy       — look up a Policy by id\ndelegatic_list_policies    — list every registered Policy\ndelegatic_delete_policy    — remove a Policy\ndelegatic_authorize        — issue a fresh AuthorizationBlock\ndelegatic_verify           — verify a block's HMAC signature + TTL"},{"id":"blk-59353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88729","text":"Remote agents (body-browser-mcp, body-os-mcp, FleetPrompt's InstallEngine, Graphonomous replay flows) call "},{"id":"spn-88730","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic_authorize"},{"id":"spn-88731","text":" to obtain the fresh blocks they need for destructive edges per OS-011 §4.4."}]},{"id":"blk-59354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88732","text":"This is the "},{"id":"spn-88733","marks":["italic"],"text":"authorization kernel"},{"id":"spn-88734","text":" — the minimum needed to close the OS-011 destructive-edge loop. The full Delegatic spec ("},{"id":"spn-88735","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic.com/docs/spec/"},{"id":"spn-88736","text":") layers on org trees, memberships, effective-policy computation, and a LiveView dashboard; those are future work."}]},{"id":"blk-59355","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88737","text":"Contract"}]},{"id":"blk-59356","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# 1. Register a policy\n:ok =\n  Delegatic.put_policy(\n    Delegatic.Policy.new(%{\n      policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n      allow_actions: [\"file_write\", \"shell_exec\"],\n      deny_actions: [\"file_delete\"],\n      agents: [\"ops-agent\"],\n      max_ttl_seconds: 300\n    })\n  )\n\n# 2. Directly request authorization for one action\n{:ok, block} =\n  Delegatic.authorize(\n    action_type: \"file_write\",\n    policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n    agent_id: \"ops-agent\",\n    approved_by: \"supervisor@acme\"\n  )\n\n# 3. Or build a function ready for the OS-011 Replay `:authorizer` slot\nauthorizer =\n  Delegatic.authorizer_for(\n    policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n    approved_by: \"supervisor@acme\",\n    agent_id: \"ops-agent\"\n  )\n\n# 4. Wire it into body-os replay\nBodyOs.Replay.execute(session, trace, authorizer: authorizer)"},{"id":"blk-59357","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88738","text":"AuthorizationBlock"}]},{"id":"blk-59358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88739","text":"Every issued block carries:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-59360","spans":[{"id":"spn-88740","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-59361","spans":[{"id":"spn-88741","text":"Example"}]}],"id":"blk-59359","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-59362","spans":[{"id":"spn-88742","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_id"}]},{"id":"blk-59363","spans":[{"id":"spn-88743","marks":["code"],"text":"\"delegatic://ws-42/ops\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-59364","spans":[{"id":"spn-88744","marks":["code"],"text":"approved_by"}]},{"id":"blk-59365","spans":[{"id":"spn-88745","marks":["code"],"text":"\"supervisor@acme\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-59366","spans":[{"id":"spn-88746","marks":["code"],"text":"approved_at"}]},{"id":"blk-59367","spans":[{"id":"spn-88747","text":"ISO8601 UTC"}]}],[{"id":"blk-59368","spans":[{"id":"spn-88748","marks":["code"],"text":"expires_at"}]},{"id":"blk-59369","spans":[{"id":"spn-88749","text":"ISO8601 UTC (capped at "},{"id":"spn-88750","marks":["code"],"text":"policy.max_ttl_seconds"},{"id":"spn-88751","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-59370","spans":[{"id":"spn-88752","marks":["code"],"text":"authorization_token"}]},{"id":"blk-59371","spans":[{"id":"spn-88753","marks":["code"],"text":"\"sha256:<64-hex>\""},{"id":"spn-88754","text":" — HMAC over the other fields"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-59372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88755","text":"The token is "},{"id":"spn-88756","marks":["italic"],"text":"tamper-evident"},{"id":"spn-88757","text":", not secret — any consumer can call "},{"id":"spn-88758","marks":["code"],"text":"Delegatic.AuthorizationBlock.verify/1"},{"id":"spn-88759","text":" to detect forgery or expiration."}]},{"id":"blk-59373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88760","text":"The HMAC key lives in "},{"id":"spn-88761","marks":["code"],"text":"config :delegatic, :hmac_key"},{"id":"spn-88762","text":". A per-process random fallback is used when unset (fine for tests, unsafe for prod)."}]},{"id":"blk-59374","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88763","text":"Policy semantics"}]},{"id":"blk-59375","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88764","marks":["bold"],"text":"`action in deny_actions`"},{"id":"spn-88765","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-88766","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :denied_by_policy}"}]}],"id":"blk-59376","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88767","marks":["bold"],"text":"`agents` set and `agent_id` not in it"},{"id":"spn-88768","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-88769","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :agent_not_allowed}"}]}],"id":"blk-59378","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59381","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88770","marks":["bold"],"text":"`action not in allow_actions`"},{"id":"spn-88771","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-88772","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :not_in_allowlist}"},{"id":"spn-88773","text":" (deny-by-default)"}]}],"id":"blk-59380","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88774","text":"Otherwise → "},{"id":"spn-88775","marks":["code"],"text":":ok"}]}],"id":"blk-59382","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-59384","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88776","text":"Wiring Delegatic into OS-011 replay"}]},{"id":"blk-59385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88777","text":"The OS-011 spec §4.4 requires that every destructive replay edge obtain a "},{"id":"spn-88778","marks":["italic"],"text":"fresh"},{"id":"spn-88779","text":" authorization — prior authorization does not carry. Delegatic's "},{"id":"spn-88780","marks":["code"],"text":"authorizer_for/1"},{"id":"spn-88781","text":" returns a function that re-issues a new block on every call, producing exactly the semantics OS-011 demands:"}]},{"id":"blk-59386","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Recorded trace: destructive edges carry OLD authorization blocks\n# Replay stripper: body-os.Replay strips them before dispatch\n# Delegatic authorizer: fresh block for every edge that makes it through policy\n# Session: enforces the destructive-action gate on the fresh block"},{"id":"blk-59387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88782","text":"See "},{"id":"spn-88783","marks":["code"],"text":"body-os/test/delegatic_integration_test.exs"},{"id":"spn-88784","text":" for the end-to-end test that exercises this flow — both the success path (allowlist policy → replay succeeds) and the failure path (readonly policy → replay halts with "},{"id":"spn-88785","marks":["code"],"text":"reason: \"authorization_failure\""},{"id":"spn-88786","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-59388","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88787","text":"Running the suite"}]},{"id":"blk-59389","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"mix deps.get\nmix test"},{"id":"blk-59390","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88788","text":"References"}]},{"id":"blk-59391","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88789","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic.com/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-88790","text":" — full v0.2 spec (organizations, memberships, effective policy, dashboard)"}]}],"id":"blk-59392","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88791","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"},{"id":"spn-88792","text":" §4.4 — AuthorizationBlock contract"}]}],"id":"blk-59394","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88793","marks":["code"],"text":"body-os/"},{"id":"spn-88794","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-88795","marks":["code"],"text":"body-browser/"},{"id":"spn-88796","text":" — OS-011 providers whose Replay flows consume Delegatic authorizers"}]}],"id":"blk-59396","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-59398","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88797","text":"License"}]},{"id":"blk-59399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88798","text":"Apache-2.0"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraxb6xlzisuyqjtmy5zo2tfwzccj7jr5wifxvzzpnfu3etenp2mj5a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}